  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "The enrichment culture was established by adding several reduced and nonreduced samples (_x0005_400 ml) of sediment and spring water to a double-walled glass vessel with a total volume of _x0005_800 ml."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "The Inoculation was performed inside a Coy anaerobic tent (Coy Laboratories) to avoid exposure to air."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Heated glycerol was pumped through the outer chamber of the vessel to maintain a constant temperature of 85°C."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "A gas mixture consisting of N2/CO2 (80:20) was constantly bubbled through the culture at a rate of 20 ml/min."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": "The anaerobic growth medium consisted of a modified Allen’s formulation (Arch Mikrobiol 32:270 –277(1959)) and was continuously added to the vessel at a rate of 8.0 ml/h using a Gilson Minipuls2 peristaltic pump (Gilson)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "Culture effluent was allowed to overflow through a side port in the cultivation vessel and into a sterile, anaerobic 2 l glass media bottle."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
